# KMP Review

## Checklist

- Business logic in `commonMain` — no Android or iOS SDK imports leaking in.
- `expect`/`actual` used for genuinely platform-specific behaviour only.
- Every `expect` has a matching `actual` in all declared targets.
- Source set dependencies correct — `commonMain` does not depend on platform sets.
- Ktor: platform engine configured (OkHttp/Darwin), timeout/retry at client level, serialization plugin set.
- No hardcoded base URLs — inject from config.
- `Dispatchers.Main` not assumed equivalent across platforms.
- `runBlocking` not used on iOS main thread.
- Flows from shared code use `StateFlow`/`SharedFlow` for iOS consumption.
- Public API Objective-C compatible where needed.
- `suspend` functions exported to Swift correctly.
- All targets build cleanly.

## Output Format

```markdown
## KMP Review Findings

**[P1]** `path/file.kt:line` - Title
Why it matters and fix direction.

## Summary
Platform boundary health verdict.
```
